<title>USA: Kellogg Q3 global volume rises 1.0 percent.</title>
<headline>Kellogg Q3 global volume rises 1.0 percent.</headline>
<dateline>BATTLE CREEK, Mich. 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kellogg Co said Friday its third quarter global volume increased by one percent to a record level, with strength in ready-to-eat cereal volume outside the United States and convenience foods volume more than offsetting continued softness in U.S. cereal.</p>
<p>&quot;As previously forecast, our third quarter performance was influenced significantly by competitive conditions in the U.S. cereal category,&quot; Arnold Langbo, chairman, said in a statement.</p>
</text>
